content.text:
Now footer visible at bottom; court barely visible (very dark). Still large blank but footer anchors. Could lighten more to reveal court; currently court border faint at bottom. The demo court is almost black due overlay .55. Maybe add a subtle line "THE COURT IS WAITING" would fill. But minimalism. It's okay though 300px blank looks like a design issue.

Maybe could make the menu content vertically centered rather than top, but the top header always at top. If content centered, blank split top/bottom. Worse maybe.

Alternative: On mobile, move the title down and space fields? Current h1 huge. Could add a "court preview" at bottom showing large demo paddles/ball above footer. We can reduce the overlay opacity bottom to .25 and move court up? Court begins at 122 behind content; paddles at center y ~? after layout top maybe 157, h? We can lighten bottom to show. It would be pretty. To avoid court content behind fields, overlay could have a gradient that is .94 until 58%, then .75, .55. Currently .73 at 74%, .55 bottom. In screenshot the court bottom shows faint, but court mostly black; its fill is dark, so even .55 overlay leaves near black. We can add a brighter court glow at bottom? Or hide the actual court and draw a decorative "ball" in the empty space. Hmm.

Maybe add a visual "SERVE" large outlined ball at bottom? CSS decorative `.menu-empty-mark` with circular glow and text. But not necessary. We could restructure menu on mobile to include the aside rule card at bottom: "5 / points wins. Walls are in. Pride is on." with the mint 5. That fills some blank and communicates. Show `.menu-aside` on mobile but style as a horizontal strip/rule at bottom, not overlap. Since menu-body currently top; foot at bottom. Could insert aside after setup inside menu-copy? It's a sibling after menu-copy within menu-body. On mobile hide aside. We can display it as a compact banner below options, making menu content to ~620. But 844 still 200 blank then footer.

Maybe include a mini instruction/rule row with "THE RULE / 5 points wins / walls are in" after base. We could reuse aside on mobile as horizontal card under setup. Add CSS:
```
@media max-width 720:
 .menu-aside {display:flex; width:100%; margin-top:18px; align-items:flex-start; ... padding:14px; flex-direction? }
```
But menu-body contains menu-copy and aside; display flex row currently; at mobile .menu-body align-items flex-start but flex direction default row; menu-copy width 100%; aside would be next to it off-screen. Need `.menu-body{flex-direction:column}` on mobile. Then aside below, width 100%; display grid or flex row. This could fill. Let's do a compact rule strip:
```
.menu-aside {
 display: grid; grid-template-columns: auto 1fr auto; width:100%; align-items:center; padding:12px 14px; margin:18px 0 0; text-align:left;
}
.aside-rule {display:none}
.aside-kicker {grid-column:1}
.aside-big {font-size:42; grid-column:1; ...}
.aside-copy {grid-column:2}
.aside-motion, .aside-foot {display:none}
```
But DOM order: aside-rule, aside-kicker, aside-big, aside-copy, aside-rule, aside-motion, aside-foot. Could hide rules/motion/foot; grid. Layout:
- kicker at top left small.
- big 5 at left below.
- copy right.
Maybe use flex:
```
.menu-aside {display:flex; flex-direction:row; align-items:center; gap:14; width:100%; ... text-align:left}
.aside-rule:first-child, .aside-motion, .aside-foot, .aside-rule:last-of-type {display:none}
.aside-kicker {display:none}
.aside-big {font-size:54px; margin:0}
.aside-copy {font-size:12px; line-height:1.4}
```
This creates a strip "5 points wins. Walls are in. Pride is on." Nice, informative, fills ~80px. Combined menu content 560. Still blank to bottom 790 (230), but footer. Could put a decorative "↕ MOVE" at right. Add aside motion? Maybe. Hmm.

Alternatively, on mobile, set menu-body min-height: 100%, and spread content: title/options at top, court rule at bottom before footer, creating negative space intentionally. The 5 strip could be at bottom of body with margin-top:auto. That would fill and anchor. But content after fields? We can place aside at bottom. flex column with body; aside margin-top auto; footer below. This would leave whitespace between setup and rule, which is fine.
- At 844: header 60, body flex 1 (from 70 to 790), menu-copy content to 480, aside at bottom 730, footer 820. Nice. The court may show behind empty. This seems polished.
- Let's implement mobile aside as a horizontal "rule card" anchored near bottom:
```
.menu-body { flex-direction: column; }
.menu-aside { display:flex; width:100%; margin-top:auto; margin-bottom:12; padding:12px 14px; gap:12px; align-items:center; text-align:left; background:...; }
.aside-rule,.aside-kicker,.aside-motion,.aside-foot {display:none}
.aside-big { font-size:52px; margin:0 650?; color mint; }
.aside-copy {font-size:12; color; line-height; }
```
- But `.menu-body` in mobile currently `align-items:flex-start; padding...`; add flex-direction column. `.menu-copy` width 100. aside width.
- If viewport short 680, content could overflow; menu-inner scrolls. Fine.
- The menu footer sits at bottom. The aside before footer. 
- This will show the 5 and rule. It is nice. 
- The aside `.aside-big` line height. 
- On mobile, maybe also show motion bar (vertical) to fill? Not needed.

- For desktop, panel remains.

- Also the gradient lightening could be reverted? Court remains dark; with aside strip that's fine. Keep.

Let's add mobile aside. Also need ensure the layout of menu-body `flex-direction` applies. In CSS `@media (max-width:720px)` menu-body not currently flex-direction. Add. Then menu-aside hidden override replace with display flex.

